{
  "id": "Compound::DB00443 - Gene::5243",
  "verbalization": "Betamethasone is implicated in the regulation of Abcb1 through a series of interconnected pathways involving glucocorticoids. The evidence suggests that Betamethasone, through its role in causing Scleral Thinning or Steroid Withdrawal Syndrome, is linked to Methylprednisolone, which binds to Abcb1. This binding is further supported by the presence of a common ancestor, Therapeutic Glucocorticoid, which links Betamethasone and Methylprednisolone to the primary alpha-hydroxy ketone. Similarly, Hydrocortisone, another glucocorticoid, also binds to Abcb1, reinforcing the role of glucocorticoids in the regulation of Abcb1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which glucocorticoids influence Abcb1 expression or function, likely through the modulation of cellular processes that involve the ABC transporter. The recurring involvement of glucocorticoids and their binding to Abcb1 suggests a broader role in drug resistance or metabolic regulation, though the exact mechanisms remain to be fully elucidated.",
